:: End1 {"position":"750,625","size":"100,100"}
The air around <<Riko>> started to move again. Her eyes blinked. She gasped.  
“<<Reg>>?! What’s happening?”  

He smiled faintly. “I think… I fixed it.”  

She tried to reach him, but his hand went through hers.  
“You’ll be fine,” he said.  

She touched one of the glowing flowers on the ground.  
“I’ll find you. No matter how deep I have to go.”  

The light faded. She walked into the next tunnel alone.


:: EscapeUp {"position":"1000,625","size":"100,100"}
They tried to climb upward. The sunlight was faint above.  
The tunnel shook beneath their feet, sending pebbles tumbling down. <<Riko>> gripped the rocks tightly, heart pounding.  
“<<Reg>>! Hold on!” she shouted, but there was no answer.  

The tunnel narrowed, forcing her to squeeze through jagged stones. Dust filled the air, making it hard to breathe. Every step was a struggle; she slipped once, catching herself just in time.  

Finally, <<Riko>> reached the top. The fresh air hit her face, but <<Reg>> wasn’t there. A faint voice called:  
> “Go. Don’t look back.”  

Tears stung her eyes. “I can’t… I can’t leave him,” she whispered.  
She glanced down at the dark tunnel below, imagining <<Reg>> struggling, or worse.  

Then she swallowed her fear, feeling a strange resolve. She had to move forward, even alone. With one last look at the opening, she climbed out, sunlight warming her face.


:: FollowCreature {"position":"1125,500","size":"100,100"}
The glowing creature led them deeper into the cave.  
They passed glowing mushrooms, their soft light casting long shadows. Underground streams murmured quietly beside them, reflecting the strange colors of the walls.  

<<Riko>> whispered, “Do you think it’s safe?”  
<<Reg>> shook his head. “I don’t know… but it hasn’t hurt us yet.”  

The creature stopped at a shimmering wall that seemed almost alive, reflecting their faces like water. It tilted its head, then vanished silently.  
<<Reg>> and <<Riko>> exchanged nervous glances. “What now?” <<Riko>> asked.  

The walls pulsed faintly, and a breeze stirred from somewhere unseen. Small glowing shapes darted in the shadows — maybe fish, maybe something else. The cave felt alive, watching them.  

<<Reg>> took a deep breath. “We move forward. Together.”  
They stepped closer to the shimmering wall, unsure if it was a door, a mirror, or a trap.


:: FollowVoice {"position":"875,625","size":"100,100"}
They followed the voice into the mist.  
A shadow waited at the end, smiling.  
<<Riko>> held <<Reg>>’s hand tight.  
“Should we trust it?” she asked.  

[[> Step forward->OpenEnding1]]
[[> Turn back->OpenEnding2]]


:: HideRocks {"position":"1000,500","size":"100,100"}
They hid behind the rocks. Something passed by — tall, thin, with glowing eyes.  
<<Reg>> whispered, “It’s gone.”  
<<Riko>> shook her head. “No. It’s waiting.”  

The ground cracked. They fell into darkness. When they woke, they were in a quiet cave with faint lights on the walls.  
A small glowing creature climbed out from a flower.  

[[> Follow the creature->FollowCreature]]
[[> Stay and rest->RestCave]]


:: OpenEnding1 {"position":"750,750","size":"100,100"}
<<Reg>> and <<Riko>> stepped forward into the mist, holding each other’s hands tight.  
The cave walls glowed faintly, as if alive, and the soft voice whispered again:  
> “This way… you must continue.”

Every step felt heavier than the last. The mist made it hard to see, but they didn’t stop. <<Riko>>’s heart pounded, and <<Reg>> could feel hers through her grip.  

They passed strange glowing plants, some moving slightly as if breathing. <<Riko>> whispered, “Do you think anyone has ever come here before?”  
<<Reg>> shook his head. “I don’t know… maybe we’re the first.”  

Suddenly, the tunnel opened into a huge cavern. Water fell from the ceiling, sparkling in pale blue light. The sound of it echoed everywhere, making them feel both tiny and scared.  

“Look!” <<Riko>> pointed at a platform in the center, floating above the water. A small glowing orb hovered above it.  
<<Reg>> swallowed. “That must be the thing calling us.”

They climbed carefully, trying not to slip on wet stone. When they reached the platform, the orb pulsed, and a warmth spread through their bodies. <<Riko>>’s hand tightened around <<Reg>>’s.  
“Do we touch it?” she asked quietly.  

<<Reg>> nodded slowly. “Together.”  

They reached out. The orb’s warmth flowed into them, making their skin tingle. Time seemed to slow. The cavern shivered around them, but they felt calm — like they had finally found a safe place.  

Then the voice spoke again, soft but firm:  
> “The choice is yours. Stay here, or go beyond.”  

<<Riko>> looked at <<Reg>>. “If we stay, we’ll be safe… but I feel like something waits for us further.”  
<<Reg>> hesitated. “I don’t know if we’re ready… but I trust you.”  

They stepped forward together. The orb lifted them gently into the air. The cavern stretched and twisted around them, glowing light reflecting on the water like stars in the sky.  

<<Riko>> laughed softly, nervous but happy. “It’s… beautiful.”  
<<Reg>> smiled, feeling the same wonder.  

The mist swallowed them completely, and the last thing they saw were the tiny glowing flowers on the platform below, fading slowly.


:: OpenEnding2 {"position":"1000,750","size":"100,100"}
They turned back, deciding the voice might be a trap. The mist thickened, and the soft whispers grew louder, almost angry.  
<<Riko>> gripped <<Reg>>’s arm. “Are we making a mistake?”  
<<Reg>> shook his head. “Maybe… but at least we’ll choose our path.”

The tunnel twisted and narrowed. The glow faded, and the sound of dripping water became louder. Every shadow looked like it could move, but nothing did.  

Suddenly, the floor cracked beneath them. <<Riko>> screamed. <<Reg>> grabbed her, pulling her back, but the stone fell away and a small hole opened in the wall. It led to another passage, dark and silent.  

They stepped through carefully. The passage sloped downward, the air colder here. <<Riko>> shivered. “It feels… alive,” she whispered.  

<<Reg>> nodded. “We just have to keep going.”  

After what felt like hours, they reached a huge chamber. Stalactites hung like jagged teeth. At the center, a pool of glowing water reflected them both. <<Riko>> approached it and touched the surface. Ripples spread, and in them, she saw faint images of places above — sunlight, forests, rivers.  

“This… is what we’re missing?” she asked.  
<<Reg>> knelt beside her. “Maybe. But maybe it’s a warning too.”  

The water shimmered and then calmed. The chamber was silent except for their breathing. <<Riko>> looked at <<Reg>>. “We can’t stop here forever. We have to move.”  

<<Reg>> nodded. They held hands and walked deeper into the darkness, their own steps the only sound.  

The faint glow of the water faded behind them, leaving the chamber empty and silent.


:: RestCave {"position":"1125,625","size":"100,100"}
They sat on the floor. The cave was quiet, the only sound their breathing and the soft hum of glowing flowers.  
<<Riko>> touched one of the flowers. “Maybe it’s safe… for now,” she whispered.  

<<Reg>> nodded. “We can rest a bit. But we can’t stay forever.”  

She looked around the cave, noticing tiny creatures moving in the shadows, glowing softly. “Do you think anyone has ever been here before?”  

<<Reg>> shook his head. “If they did… they didn’t leave any traces we can see.”  

They shared a small smile. Even in the darkness, they found comfort in each other.  
<<Riko>> leaned back, letting the soft glow wash over her face. “I almost forgot how peaceful it can feel… even down here.”  

<<Reg>> sighed, resting his metal arm across his knees. “Peace… but only for a moment. We have to keep going eventually.”  

Outside the circle of glowing flowers, the cave seemed darker, deeper, unknown. Their rest ended not with fear, but with quiet resolve.


:: Start {"position":"875,375","size":"100,100"}
<<Reg>> was running. His steps echoed through the tunnel, mixed with <<Riko>>’s quick breathing behind him. The air felt heavy and warm, and something was roaring far away. He didn’t know what it was. He didn’t want to find out.

“Keep going!” <<Riko>> shouted. Her voice cracked on the last word.  
“I’m trying!” he said, his metal arm shaking as he pulled her along.

The light from his hand flickered weakly, and the walls around them looked alive. Rocks fell from the ceiling, one almost hitting his shoulder.

Then, the tunnel split into three paths.  

<<Riko>> stopped, panting. “Which way?”  
<<Reg>> looked around helplessly. “They all look the same!”

The ground trembled again. Dust rained down. The roar came closer.  

<<Riko>> didn’t wait. “Middle one!” she said, and they ran together.

After a few seconds, the sound behind them stopped. The ground was still. Only silence.  

The new cave opened into a huge room. A soft blue glow floated in the middle. It looked like a star trapped underground.  

“What is that?” <<Riko>> whispered.  

<<Reg>> stepped closer. “Maybe… something that can help us?”  
She shook her head. “Or something that kills us.”

He smiled a little. “Let’s find out.”

[[> Touch the light->TouchLight]]
[[> Stay back and watch->StayBack]]
[[> Hide behind the rocks->HideRocks]]


:: StayBack {"position":"875,500","size":"100,100"}
<<Reg>> pulled his hand back. “No. It’s too strange.”  
<<Riko>> nodded. “Yeah… maybe it’s dangerous.”

The light floated closer to them. A soft voice came from it:  
> “Go deeper. It’s waiting.”  

“Deeper?” <<Riko>> said quietly. “What’s waiting?”  
The light faded, leaving only a soft wind.  

[[> Follow the voice->FollowVoice]]
[[> Turn back->EscapeUp]]


:: TouchLight {"position":"750,500","size":"100,100"}
The moment his fingers touched the light, it spread up his arm like cold fire. His chest hurt, like something was trying to crawl inside.

“<<Reg>>!” <<Riko>> screamed. She grabbed his shoulder, but everything froze.  
Literally froze.

The only thing moving now was the light. It filled him with strange warmth. His heartbeat slowed and sped up at the same time.  

Then a voice spoke inside his head:  
> “The gate must open.”  

<<Reg>> gasped. “Who said that?”  
No one answered.  

The voice came again:  
> “You are the key.”  

<<Reg>> looked at <<Riko>>. Her face was frozen. He reached out, but his hand passed through her.  

The light pulsed once, circles of pale blue spread under him.  

The voice said:  
> “One must rise. One must stay.”

He looked at <<Riko>> again. “If staying saves her… then I’ll stay.”  

The light grew brighter, swallowing him. His body faded into glowing pieces of light.  

[[> The Light Within->End1]]


